			"text": "was predicted (Ref. 8). The distinction between flame spread and regression is important when one considers the classic limiting O2 index test (Ref. 9), where a small sample is burned like a candle flame in a 4-cm/s oxidizer flow velocity, and the O2 concentration is reduced until the flame extinguishes. The small flames in 1g sit at the top of the sample instead of spreading down the sample near the extinction limit. A similar shaped flame is observed at very low O2 concentration in the space experiment, as shown in Figure 4.4(f). The flame survived under the low-O2 conditions until the initially hemispherical rod tip regressed to a flat surface. It never spread along the outer surface of the rod."
