			"text": "Figure 4.4.-Two flame sequences showing very different burning behavior. Black polymethylmethacrylate (PMMA) rod, 4.76 mm, 18.5 percent O2, with decreasing flow at (a) 1.9 cm/s, (b) 1.7 cm/s, (c) 1.6 cm/s, and (d) 1.5 cm/s. (e) Posttest rod, showing general conical burn shape except blunt melted tip of the rod. (f) Black PMMA rod, 3.18 mm, 16.3 percent O2, at 5 cm/s. Cap-shaped flame burned away initial hemispherical tip of rod to flat surface and then extinguished. The postburn rod samples in Figure 4.5 preserve bubble layers for the opposed flow and for concurrent flow (Olson tests)."
