			"text": "Figure 7.4.-Steady flame spread rate for both 2.2- and 1.2-cm-wide samples. Figure 7.5 shows a typical flame quenching sequence in the BASS-II experiment. A 2.2-cm-wide sample in 18.7 percent O2 was first ignited at 10-cm/s flow. Flow speed was decreased to 2.2 cm/s incrementally after ignition. Figure 7.6 shows flame tracking and flow speed versus time. After ignition, the flame started to grow. As the flow speed was reduced, both flame length and flame width dropped accordingly with flow. After 25 s, flow velocity was reduced to 2.2 cm/s and held there for the remainder of the test. As shown in Figure 7.5, both the flame length and flame width continued to decrease approaching a circular-shaped blue flame seen from the top."
