			"text": "D.7 Appendix-Polymethylmethacrylate Growth to Steady Size In Figure D.6, a one-sided PMMA slab was burned at a slow flow. The 1-cm-wide sample took 7.5 min for the total test time, with the ignition taking over 1 min. Flame reached steady size in about 3 min and was only 15 mm long. The spread rate was 0.037 mm/s (0.0037 cm/s or 2.2 mm/min). The BASS 1-cm sphere had an initial mass of 617.5 mg. Sample 19 (1-cm PMMA sphere) was completely consumed in four tests (various high- and low-flow speeds) with the burn durations in Table D.2. The total burn time was 5 min and 25 s (325 s). The average burning rate was 617.5/325 = 1.9 mg/s. Assume this occurs over the surface of the sphere where A = 4πr2 = 3.14 × 0.52 × 4 = 3.14 cm2."
