			"text": "Flammability of Materials on the Moon Jennifer Zayac1,2, Michael Johnston2, Gary Ruff 2 and Paul Ferkul2,3 1Ohio Northern University, Ada, OH, 2National Aeronautics and Space Administration, Cleveland, Ohio, Universities Space Research Association, Cleveland, OH The spaceflight unit of Flammability of Materials on the Moon (FM2) will add various features and upgrades to increase free internal volume, hardened systems for space travel, and facilitate communications to the lander, then Earth. Introduction •Onboard Gas Cylinders •Pressure/temperature sensors •Single trigger PLC controlled •Two Color Cameras •LED Illumination •Four Independent Ignitors Key Features This work was made possible by the funding provided by Biological and Physical Sciences (BPS and )Mars Campaign Office (MCO) as"
