			"text": "Ignitors Key Features This work was made possible by the funding provided by Biological and Physical Sciences (BPS and )Mars Campaign Office (MCO) as well as the Staff at the Zero Gravity Research Facility staff and Dan Gotti for building the engineering unit. ZIN Technologies will build the flight unit to fly on a Human Lander System (HLS). Intern funding has been provided by the NASA Mars Campaign Office, NASA Biological and Physical Sciences division, and the Ohio Space Grant Consortium. Acknowledgements The flame tip opens as the chamber loses oxygen and near extinction, allowing a greater amount of oxygen to flow through the middle, letting the flame burn a little longer. As the oxygen begins to deplete, the flame becomes smaller and turns blue just before extinction."
